From b0638c8daca508569ac343f58828243c10294c6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:10:30 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Route rebuilds of special buffers with history through
 a normal replace

bufferResetRows kept the history, so a special buffer that was made writable,
edited and rebuilt replayed stale records.  A rebuild is now an ordinary replace
when the buffer has history, and unchanged when it has none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01947MBgCkoERXfoyRGfCmQi
